 due to award in Q1 2027.\n- Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2 2027.\n- VLTX holdings won 60% of the last tender round.\n- VLTX utility order intake has risen every quarter, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$670M in 2026Q3. That is about 10% higher over three quarters.\n\n**Data centres (still growing, but slower)**\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than 2026. Power availability is limiting new sites.\n- The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months. The long wait suggests a backlog that supports demand, but also a cap on how fast it can convert into orders.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The utility figures are plans. Whether they get financed is a separate question. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, and two utility share offerings were cut back in size. n3 is covering this.\n- I did not find 2026 baseline spending in dollars or VLTX's customer mix, so I can't size the dollar increase.","ttft_ms":1527,"type":"result","duration_ms":34599,"uuid":"826945f5-cdf0-4e37-ad15-73b82a36297d","ttft_stream_ms":933,"time_to_request_ms":154,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":15,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":5,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":23,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":12,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":23,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":11,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":101,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":58,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":173,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":98,"process_rss_mib_result":192,"process_anon_mib_result":110,"process_peak_rss_mib":193,"process_cpu_ms_turn":556,"proce